 = filmmaking.\n\nLet’s fill in everything:\n\n| Position | Job            | Movie     | Hobby       |\n|----------|----------------|-----------|-------------|\n| 1        | police-officer | adventure | collecting  |\n| 2        | journalist     | thriller  | filmmaking  |\n\nNow check all constraints:\n\n- Journalist (pos 2) is to the right of adventure (pos 1) → ✅\n- Police-officer (pos 1) ≠ filmmaking (pos 2) → ✅ (they are different people)\n\nAll attributes are uniquely assigned.\n\nNow answer the questions:\n\n1. **At what position is the person who watches adventure?**  \n   → Position 1\n\n2. **What hobby does the person who is a journalist do?**  \n   → Journalist is in position 2 → hobby = filmmaking\n\n3. **What is the job of the person who watches adventure?**  \n   → Adventure is in position 1 → job = police-officer\n\n4. **What is the job of the person who watches thriller?**  \n   → Thriller is in position 2 → job = journalist\n\nSo the four answers are:\n1. 1\n2. filmmaking\n3. police-officer\n4. journalist\n\nFinal answer format:\n\n<solution>1, filmmaking, police-officer, journalist</solution>\n\nFinal answer: <solution>1, filmmaking, police-officer, journalist</solution>", "logprobs": [{"token": "We", "logprob": -0.07889051735401154}, {"token": " are", "logprob": -0.07899627089500427}, {"token": " told", "logprob": -0.9740785360336304}, {"token": " there", "logprob": -0.20525512099266052}, {"token": " are", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " two", "logprob": -0.3927827775478363}, {"token": " people", "logprob": -2.50339189733495e-06}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -0.005950355436652899}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.0006491222884505987}, {"token": " line", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.0006486457423307002}, {"token": " numbered", "logprob": -0.03614849969744682}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -0.03978721797466278}, {"token": "1", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " (", "logprob": -0.008629413321614265}, {"token": "left", "logprob":